Package: memga
Type: Package
Title: Multiple Choice Method for Selecting Sets of Alternatives
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sérgio Augusto Faria", "Salles", , "safsalles@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Henrique Rego Monteiro", "da Hora", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Selects a set of alternatives that complement each other, instead of
    ranking the alternatives one by one. Implements the Multiple Choice Method
    ('MEM') proposed in da Hora and Costa (2015)
    <doi:10.1590/0103-6513.084812>, which scores a set by the share of
    criteria combinations in which the set reaches a cutoff, and an adaptation
    that scores criteria in pairs using the weaker criterion of each pair. The
    best set is found either by exhaustive search, which ranks every
    combination, or by a genetic algorithm for problems too large to enumerate,
    with an optional number of vacancies per group. Includes radar charts to
    compare sets and two simulated recruiting data sets.
